america's inflation surge continues a  new report shows prices on everyday  items jumped in june with the largest  increase in more than 40 years it's  hitting one particular group the hardest  [Applause]  [Music]  amazon has a catchy song to promote its  annual prime day which offers thousands  of deals  [Music]  [Applause]  but the sale comes as the cost of living  hit a sour note consumer prices jumped  9.1 percent in june the largest increase  in four decades a look inside the  numbers shows the cost of rent rose at a  rate not seen since 1991.  prices at the grocery store saw the  largest one-year increase since 1979  and gas soared nearly 60 percent in the  month of june it really impacts lower  household incomes much more dramatically  than anyone else  cbs news business analyst jill  schlesinger says the high prices are  making it difficult for many americans  to make ends meet don't forget a lot of  americans have used the excess savings  that they accumulated during the  pandemic stimulus checks unemployment  benefits there is a bit of good news the  cost of gas is dropping aaa says price  is down almost 40 cents a gallon in the  past month but drivers like joanne ward  tell us it still costs too much to fill  up i mean any little bit is good but  we could be paying a whole lot less  the federal reserve expected to once  again raise interest rates later this  month in an attempt to ease price hikes  but there will not be an immediate  effect it can really lag so the impact  of those rate increases takes a while to  trickle through the economy schlesinger  says inflation may not start to ease  until the fall
 

